# Lifecycle and change management

Read `docs/project/project.md` → **Lifecycle stage** before large refactors or schema changes.

## Lifecycle stages

| Stage | Refactor bar |
|-------|----------------|
| **MVP** | Rigorous refactors OK; breaking changes need migration notes in PR |
| **Live** | ADR or explicit plan; migrations; prefer additive changes; extended smoke |
| **Mature** | Stricter; feature flags for risky rollout; staging smoke for XL |

## When specs drift

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Issue spec wrong mid-work | Update `docs/project/issues/<n>/spec.md` + issue comment; ADR if architectural |
| Product pivot | Update `project.md` + `roadmap.md`; supersede ADRs |
| Issue closes | **Update `roadmap.md`** (required) |

Record deltas in issue spec **Change log** section.

## Refactor triggers

- **MVP:** proceed with tests green; note in PR.
- **Live:** stop if no ADR/migration plan for breaking change; escalate to human.
- **Mature:** same as Live + consider feature flag (see `project.md` Delivery requirements).

## Epic closure

Dedicated subtask: all children closed, phase rubric PASS, roadmap updated, optional retrospective in `docs/project/retrospectives/`.